# The bulk value wins locally: the owner ranks the bulk entry it was born with
# above the point writes made before the switch, as 10.2.0's origin does while
# the pre-existing row is stranded (or as dropping the superseded row would).
# Every WAL reader applies those writes at their real versions, so the origin
# and its replicas disagree on the key for good.
MODULE: ContestedKeyAgreesBulkWinsLocally
TARGET: ContestedKeyAgrees
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the owner resolves a contested key to the bulk value over a point write made before the switch
PERTURBS: Create

--- FIND
OwnerRank(a) == LwwRank({o \in cache[a] : o <= rp[a]})
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: point writes made before the switch are outranked by the bulk entry.
OwnerRank(a) == LwwRank({o \in cache[a] : o <= rp[a] /\ author[o] \notin {PreAuthor, Foreign}})
--- END